wikipedia_extract: Ushio (潮, "Tide") was the twentieth of twenty-four Fubuki-class
  destroyers that were built for the Imperial Japanese Navy following World War I.
  Ushio was the only destroyer of the 20 ship strong Fubuki-class destroyers, the
  first modern destroyer class in history, to survive World War II and was the only
  ship out of the 22 combat ships involved in the Pearl Harbor assault force to survive
  post-war.  Ushio's only significant naval victory came by scoring primary credit
  for finishing off the badly damaged submarine USS Perch on 2-3 March 1942. She was
  sold for scrap in 1948.
